{"name":"Wet River Rock","hex":"#897870","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Perai."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made up of liquid or moisture, usually (but not always) water.","Of an object, etc.: covered or impregnated with liquid, usually (but not always) water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wet"},{"term":"river","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large and often winding stream which drains a land mass, carrying water down from higher areas to a lower point, oftentimes ending in another body of water, such as an ocean or in an inland sea.","Any large flow of a liquid in a single body."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To improve one’s hand to beat another player on the final card in a poker game."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/river"},{"term":"rock","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A formation of minerals, specifically:\n  The naturally occurring aggregate of solid mineral matter that constitutes a significant part of the earth's crust.","The naturally occurring aggregate of solid mineral matter that constitutes a significant part of the earth's crust."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To pelt with rocks; to stone."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rock"}],"entries":[{"title":"River Rock Casino Resort","blocks":[{"text":"River Rock Casino Resort is casino hotel located in Richmond, British Columbia along the Fraser River. Owned by Great Canadian Entertainment, the River Rock has historically been BC's largest and most profitable casino. The casino offers 80 table games and 1,150 electronic gaming machines, as well as a poker room and off-track betting parlour. The hotel has a total of 396 rooms, including standard rooms and suites, as well as a 144-berth marina."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/River_Rock_Casino_Resort_Logo.jpg/330px-River_Rock_Casino_Resort_Logo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/River_Rock_Casino_Resort","wikidata":"Q7337769"},{"title":"River","blocks":[{"text":"A river is a natural stream of fresh water that flows on land or inside caves towards another body of water at a lower elevation, such as an ocean, lake, or another river. A river may run dry before reaching the end of its course if it runs out of water, or only flow during certain seasons. Rivers are regulated by the water cycle, the processes by which water moves around the Earth. Water first enters rivers through precipitation, whether from rainfall, the runoff of water down a slope, the melting of glaciers or snow, or seepage from aquifers beneath the surface of the Earth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pirogue_running_on_the_Mekong_at_golden_hour_between_Don_Det_and_Don_Khon_Laos.jpg/330px-Pirogue_running_on_the_Mekong_at_golden_hour_between_Don_Det_and_Don_Khon_Laos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/River","wikidata":"Q4022"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Riverrockcasino-2.jpg/500px-Riverrockcasino-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Riverrockcasino-2.jpg/1280px-Riverrockcasino-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Riverrockcasino-2.jpg/500px-Riverrockcasino-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARiverrockcasino-2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/River_Rock_Casino_Resort_lobby_2026.jpg/500px-River_Rock_Casino_Resort_lobby_2026.jpg?utm_source=en.wi